*20
/    QUESTIONS:
/1. WHICH OF THE FOLLOWING GROUPS WERE NOT DISCUSSED
/(A) WHITE TENANT FARMERS
/(B) BLACK SHARECROPPERS
/(C) MEXICAN MIGRANT WORKERS
/(D) APPALACHIAN MOUNTAIN PEOPLE
	C
/2. THE ATTITUDES OF WELL-EDUCATED PEOPLE TOWARDS RURAL
/   POOR WERE DESCRIBED AS
/(A) SYMPATHETIC, CONDESCENDING
/(B) SYMPATHETIC, MISGUIDED
/(C) UNSYMPATHETIC
/(D) SUPPORTIVE, WELL-WISHING
	D
/3. WHICH ASPECT OF THE RURAL POOR LIFESTYLE IS HARDEST
/   TO UNDERSTAND
/(A) THEIR LANGUAGE
/(B) THEIR FAITH
/(C) THEIR MUSIC
/(D) THEIR ENDURANCE FOR HARDSHIP
	B
/4. WHAT IMPRESSED THE AUTHOR MOST ABOUT CHURCH SERVICES?
/(A) ITS PHYSICAL DEMANDS
/(B) THE SERMONS
/(C) THE SINGING
/(D) THE PRAYERS
	A
/5. WHICH OF THE FOLLOWING WERE THE RURAL POOR NOT
/   DESCRIBED AS KNOWING?
/(A) "SORENESS OF MIND AND BODY"
/(B) "RESIGNATION" AND "ESTRANGEMENT"
/(C) "SELF-DOUBT" AND "ABANDONMENT"
/(D) "MISERY" AND "CONVICTION"
	D
/6. WHAT COMPARISON WAS MADE IN THE STORY
/(A) THE SHARECROPPER^S LIFE TO CHRIST^S LIFE
/(B) THE VISION OF HEAVEN TO A THIRSTY MAN^S VISION
/    OF WATER
/(C) BOTH (A) AND (B)
/(D) NEITHER (A) NOR (B)
	C
/7. THE OUTSIDER^S SYMPATHY WAS SAID TO
/(A) DWELL ON SUPERFICIAL PROBLEMS
/(B) BE HYPOCRITICAL
/(C) BE PRESUMPTUOUS
/(D) ALL OF THE ABOVE
	A
/8. THE "GNAWING SUSPICION" DESCRIBED WAS THAT
/(A) OUTSIDE SYMPATHY WOULD INTERFERE
/(B) JUSTICE MIGHT NEVER BE DONE
/(C) GOD^S WILL WAS NOT BEING DONE
/(D) THE POOR WOULD EVENTUALLY LOSE FAITH
	B
/9. THE AUTHOR^S FEELING AT THE END OF THE ARTICLE WAS
/(A) DESPAIRING
/(B) EMPATHY AND A SENSE OF BEING WARNED
/(C) DISGUST FOR MISPLACED SYMPATHY
/(D) A REBORN DESIRE TO HELP
	B
/10. HOW WAS THE POOR^S FAITH DESCRIBED
/(A) REAL ZEALOTRY
/(B) OPIATED AND DELUDED
/(C) LUSTY, DRIVEN, SENSUAL
/(D) ANIMATED SPIRIT
	D
